  "query_preview": "..(Tuesday night through Sunday) \nIssued at 745 AM EDT MON APR 20 2026\n\nThe long term period will start with WNW flow aloft while ridging\napproaches from the west. A cold front will be struggling to make\nsouthward progress through IL/IN/OH as it loses momentum ahead of\nthe approaching ridge. Moisture advection will occur ahead of the\nfront, and will probably allow for shower/thunderstorm development\nnear the front. Won't rule out some of these making it into our\nnortheast counties, but they are more likely closer to the front.\nThe front doesn't make it here and mild and dry weather should\nlast from Wednesday night into Friday as the upper ridge arrives.\n\nThe ridge aloft is expected to weaken as a couple of shortwaves\ncoming out of a western CONUS trough ripple through it. This\nshould finally allow for some rain during the weekend, but the \ndetails of how it unfolds are likely to change.",
